{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: John Newton}
{genre: folk}
{tempo: 90}
# Historical text: Olney Hymns (1779), Book I, hymn XLI.
# Original simplified chord accompaniment for MusicMaestro; no modern recording arrangement.
{c:Verse 1}
[G]Amazing grace! how [C]sweet the [G]sound,
That saved a wretch like [D]me!
I [G]once was lost, but [C]now am [G]found,
Was [Em]blind, but [D]now I [G]see.

{c:Verse 2}
'Twas [G]grace that taught my [C]heart to [G]fear,
And grace my fears [D]relieved;
How [G]precious did that [C]grace [G]appear,
The [Em]hour I [D]first [G]believed!

{c:Verse 3}
Through [G]many dangers, [C]toils and [G]snares,
I have already [D]come;
'Tis [G]grace has brought me [C]safe thus [G]far,
And [Em]grace will [D]lead me [G]home.
